From: ROCKNIX beryllium port
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: beryllium: disable slpi and cdsp remoteprocs

The sensor DSP (slpi) and compute DSP (cdsp) are not used by ROCKNIX. On
beryllium the slpi firmware crash-loops ("USER-PD DOG detects stalled
initialization") every ~40s and its glink/fastrpc endpoint then re-probes and
fails with -22 in a tight storm, starving userspace (D-Bus/systemd) and stalling
the boot. We only need adsp (audio), so disable slpi and cdsp. This stops the
crash loop and the fastrpc -22 flood.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-xiaomi-beryllium-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-xiaomi-beryllium-common.dtsi
@@ -371,7 +371,7 @@
 };

 &cdsp_pas {
-	status = "okay";
+	status = "disabled";
 	firmware-name = "qcom/sdm845/Xiaomi/beryllium/cdsp.mbn";
 };

@@ -631,7 +631,7 @@
 &slpi_pas {
 	firmware-name = "qcom/sdm845/Xiaomi/beryllium/slpi.mbn";

-	status = "okay";
+	status = "disabled";
 };

 &sound {
